}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{13}=2\\sqrt{13}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1069 "q-16458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2a/2adb84964a605495c84921943ec76f9820ba18851cda817037dd6022808d1fd7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fbef9b7-68b9-5b6d-beff-b38a63574b1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434278 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1069 "q-279167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1071 "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb8398f9-e97a-58eb-bd8b-b49ccd2d689d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434279 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434280 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "54f488a2-5ee1-5f4b-9b2d-7bfa683c828f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434280 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434281 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434281 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5892bfa8-ea88-5074-97ec-8c9cbbf249ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434281 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186342039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434282 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434282 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "79a4f735-1f4e-5bcc-bb32-263a73f8784e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434282 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434283 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434283 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b18ed940-7683-5b5f-9c24-6ca0a2adfa96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434283 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434284 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434284 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e66467af-9a14-51f4-92e2-3d41e87b4f10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434284 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284499 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
